{
 "subtitle": "8 finished runs, 1.1M env steps each, size50m, one training seed per run. Scored with tools/death_eval.py on the same fixed evaluation worlds. Updated 2026-10-01.",
 "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over the evaluation episodes, and each unlock rate is the share of episodes in which that achievement fired. Every run was scored on the same fixed evaluation worlds. Re-scoring the old 5.80 record and the 2.30 run with today's code reproduced both exactly, so the differences below come from the trained policies, not from how they were measured.\nThe non-cheating model (Honest map, trained only on what the agent saw, position dead-reckoned from its own actions) scores 5.87, level with the privileged control's 5.93. Removing the privileged supervision cost nothing measurable.\nThe control never makes a pickaxe (0 of 30 episodes) and makes a sword in 60%. The honest run, with the same recipe and death fixes, makes both in 20%. So the fixes did not remove the pickaxe; which crafting key a run settles on looks like run-to-run variation or valid-action suppression.\nEvery map run unlocks WAKE_UP (sleep, then wake) in 83-98% of episodes; vanilla never does. Without it the fixed map model scores 4.20 against vanilla's 4.44; the potential runs stay above vanilla (4.90-5.03).\nSurvival never moved: lifespans 243-294 steps against 261-284 for a random policy. The honest run drinks most reliably of any map run (83%) but lives shortest (243), with half its deaths to mobs or lava.",
 "table_note": "eps = evaluation episodes. ach. = mean episode-final achievements; w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. Rates are % of episodes. 'bug' = imag_shift True, which corrupted the policy gradient (fixed 2026-09-20). map_survive was re-evaluated on 2026-09-28 and reproduced its original 2.30. One training seed per run, so the run-to-run spread is unknown. 'Map + potential (fixed)' is the old 5.80 record; 'Control' adds the recipe and death fixes with the privileged map; 'Honest map' has the same fixes with observation-only targets.",
